## Drinks

- drink normal amounts during the day, but less before bed
- cut down on tea, coffee, fizzy drinks and alcohol

## At night

Get up slowly, and use a night light to avoid falls.

## Going out

Plan toilet stops. A **Radar key** opens thousands of accessible toilets. See [accessible toilets](/support/leisure/accessible-toilets/).

## Keep an eye on changes

See a GP if your symptoms get worse, you see blood in your pee, or you have pain.

## Support

**Prostate Cancer UK** has specialist nurses who can answer questions about all prostate problems, not just cancer.
